# Repo-root ignores.
#
# This working directory has accumulated files belonging to other projects and
# to individual machines. They are listed here so that `git add -A` cannot
# sweep them into a commit — not because they are unimportant, but because
# they are not part of the Selv wardrobe app and do not belong in its history.

# --- Other projects living in this directory -------------------------------
# `trading/` is a separate quantitative research project (MR-1 mean reversion:
# strategy config, cached OHLC data, pytest artifacts). NaviBuild is a
# different business entirely — a 3D-printing financial model. Neither has any
# relationship to this app; committing them would publish unrelated business
# data to this repo.
/trading/
/NaviBuild-Base-Case.csv
/NaviBuild-Financial-Model.html

# --- Machine-local configuration -------------------------------------------
# .mcp.json wires up an MCP server by ABSOLUTE PATH on one developer's machine
# (C:/Users/.../my-vault/...). It is meaningless on any other checkout and
# leaks a local filesystem layout, so it stays untracked.
.mcp.json

# Stray empty lockfile at the repo root. The real one is app/package-lock.json;
# this one has no packages and exists only because npm was once run one
# directory too high.
/package-lock.json

# --- OS / editor -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
